messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D".\n####\n# Context:\nCanadian scientists have developed a device that allows people to generate electricity and store it through jaw movement when talking or eating. The subjects chewed gum for 60 seconds after wearing the device. The cord close to the chin generated about 10 to 18 microwatts of electricity, while each chewing during meals produced an average of about 7 microwatts. It is expected that this improved power generation method may be used to charge small electronic devices such as hearing aids, intelligent hearing protectors and even mobile phones in the future.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is inconsistent with the original text?\n# Options:\nA) The newly developed power generation method can be used to charge hearing aids.\nB) Canadian scientists have developed a device that enables the body to generate and store electricity through exercise.\nC) Chewing gum continuously for 60 seconds can generate 10-18 microwatts of electricity.\nD) People can generate electricity by talking or eating.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
