messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D".\n####\n# Context:\nAn elementary school applied to the local administrative department of education to purchase an additional school bus to strengthen the ability to transport teachers and students. The administrative department of education rejected this application on the grounds that the number of school buses must match the size of the school and the number of teachers and students .According to the current number and scale of the school\'s teachers and students, the existing school buses are enough.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following assumptions can best support the decision of the education administrative department?\n# Options:\nA) Survey shows that renting a school bus is more economical than buying a school bus\nB) Among the school buses of this elementary school, at least no vehicles will be scrapped in the near future\nC) The number of primary school-age children in this area will not increase much in the future\nD) The education administrative department has no plan to expand the scale of teachers and students of the school\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
