messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D".\n####\n# Context:\nAt present, the average fuel consumption per 100 kilometers of automobiles in our country is over 20% more than that of developed countries. Studies have shown that diesel vehicles have 20% to 30% lower fuel consumption compared with gasoline vehicles. Under the situation of serious pollutant emissions from automobiles, the development of advanced diesel vehicles can make no increase in vehicle pollutants emissions or even emission reductions. In our country, diesel vehicles account for 23.7% of the number of vehicles and only 0.2% of the number of cars. Assuming that the proportion of diesel vehicles in passenger vehicles in 2020 is 30%, and the corresponding proportion in the total vehicle ownership is 39.7%, 28.37 million tons of crude oil can be saved in 2020.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options best supports the above statement?\n# Options:\nA) It is suggested that adopting a differential tax rate for gasoline and diesel can make the price of diesel lower than that of gasoline.\nB) Encourage more people to use energy-saving products such as diesel cars.\nC) The diesel quality standards should be improved, and price monitoring methods should be used to encourage the production of high-quality diesel.\nD) Enhance the independent innovation capability of advanced diesel technology and develop advanced diesel vehicles.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
