messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D".\n####\n# Context:\nAviation Analyst: To combat human error involved in air traffic control, Miro Jets Inc. has recently installed each of its DC-10 passenger planes with a special anti-collision device. The device alerts the DC-10, via a red light, when another plane is slightly more than three minutes away from a potential collision. The red light comes on and stays on until the approaching plane is safely out of range. Aviation experts at Miro Jet Inc. have determined that three minutes is ample time for a plane to divert its respective flight path to avoid a collision. Ttherefore, if the red light on the anti-collision device is off, the DC-10 is more than three minutes flying time from any plane.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, most fundamentally calls into question the aviation analyst\'s argument?\n# Options:\nA) Recently, a near collision in which both planes were less than 90 seconds flying distance from each other was averted only by the prompt actions of air traffic controllers.\nB) When two dc-10\'s approach each other the red lights on each aircraft do not necessarily turn on simultaneously.\nC) Some aviation experts warn that in certain cases three minutes may not provide sufficient time for aircrafts to maneuver without causing on board injuries.\nD) The anti-collision device only signals planes of oncoming directions, not those planes that are flying in parallel.\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
