messages:  [['Please reason step by step to solve the logical reasoning problem. After completing the your step-by-step reasoning process, give your final answer in the following format: "\\nThe correct option is: A/B/C/D".\n####\n# Context:\nTwo hundred mice of the same kind and none of them had leukemia were exposed to some kind of radiation of the same dose and intensity, and then half of the mice were not restricted to eat the food they normally eat. and the other half gave them the same food, but in a limited amount. It was found that 55 mice in the former group had leukemia, while only 3 mice in the latter group had leukemia.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, it can be seen that which of the following is correct?\n# Options:\nA) Whether exposed to some kind of radiation or not, letting mice eat the food they normally eat increases the likelihood of leukemia\nB) For any kind of mouse, leukemia has nothing to do with exposure to some kind of radiation\nC) By controlling the amount of food these mice eat, they are less likely to develop leukemia from certain radiation exposure\nD) Mice exposed to some kind of radiation are bound to develop leukemia in the end\n\n# Instruction:\n## Reasoning:', '. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
